{%- comment -%}
  GapFinder Storefront Tracker — app embed block.

  Once a merchant installs GapFinder and enables this embed in their theme
  editor (Theme → App embeds → toggle "GapFinder Storefront Tracker"), the
  script below loads on every page and captures every storefront search:
  what shoppers typed, how many results came back, whether they clicked.

  No PII is captured — only the query string, result count, and a timestamp.
  See https://gapfinder.solnix.store/methodology for full details.

  ⚠️ The script src below is hard-coded and CANNOT be derived at render time —
  an app embed block has no access to the app's own URL. It must always match
  SHOPIFY_APP_URL / the Coolify FQDN. If they drift, the tracker 503s on every
  storefront and search capture stops dead with no error surfaced in the app.
  Re-domaining the app means editing this line AND running `shopify app deploy`
  — a web redeploy alone will not update it.

  Do NOT rename this file: tracker status detection matches on the block handle
  (`blocks/tracker/`), which is what keeps detection working across renames.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% if block.settings.enabled %}
  <script
    src="https://gapfinder.solnix.store/tracker.js"
    defer
    data-gapfinder="storefront-tracker"
  ></script>
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "GapFinder Tracker",
  "target": "head",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enabled",
      "label": "Enable storefront search tracking",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Captures shopper search queries to surface revenue gaps. Required for GapFinder to work."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
